    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test suite in the project, and both its tests pass (`Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` field: `EMAIL` when an owner has an email address, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nFollowing the existing pattern for the other derived read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `locality`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string property (enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits the field and its `OwnerDto.ContactPreferenceEnum` on the generated DTO.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping(target = \"contactPreference\", expression = \"java(toContactPreference(owner))\")` to `toOwnerDto`, plus the `toContactPreference` helper that returns `EMAIL` when `owner.getEmail()` is present (non-null, non-blank) and `PHONE` otherwise.\n\nThe value is derived purely at mapping time from the owner's email, so no entity or persistence changes were needed.",
